{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_a6d398a0f3279b1c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"bonsai2-27b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bug: `while start < end` is excluding the endpoint. The documented contract says \"count both endpoint dates.\" So it should be `while start <= end`.\n\nLet me verify with the tests:\n- test_same_weekday: business_days(2026-11-2, 2026-11-2) == 1. With `start < end`, the loop never executes → 0. With `start <= end`, start==end, weekday of 2026-11-2 is Monday (weekday 0), so count = 1. ✓\n- test_week: 2026-11-2 (Mon) to 2026-11-6 (Fri): inclusive count = 5. With `start < end`: only counts Mon–Thu = 4. With `start <= end`: 5. ✓\n- test_holiday: 2026-11-2 to 2026-11-6, holiday 2026-11-4 (Wednesday). Inclusive: Mon, Tue, Thu, Fri = 4. ✓\n- test_reversed: raises ValueError. ✓\n\nSo the fix is: change `while start < end:` to `while start <= end:`.\n\nNote: 2026-11-2 — let me confirm it's a Monday. November 2026: Nov 1, 2026 is a Sunday. So Nov 2 is Monday. Yes.\n\nMake the minimal edit and run the tests.\n","signature":"msg_a6d398a0f3279b1c"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"cache_creation":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":1773,"inference_geo":null,"input_tokens":701,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":342},"server_tool_use":{"web_fetch_requests":0,"web_search_requests":0},"service_tier":null},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c7ce0f8-8e81-4326-b36a-5aabbda5e7f1","uuid":"678ef051-689f-4c9b-8b7b-d453ed72f3f6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T10:57:01.087Z","request_id":"msg_a6d398a0f3279b1c","thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
